                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p>Dr. Mukesh Kumar obtained his B. Tech. (Agricultural Engineering) and M. Tech. (Soil and Water Engineering) from Punjab Agricultural University, Ludhiana. He received his Ph.D. in Agricultural Engineering with specialization in Soil and Water Conservation Engineering from Indian Agricultural Research Institute, New Delhi. He has more than 18 years’ experience in Teaching and Research and Extension in the area of Watershed Management, Water Management and Drip Irrigation. Presently he is working as Professor in Indira Gandhi National Open University, New Delhi. He has made significant contribution in designing course curriculum of various educational programmes at different levels viz. awareness,  certificate, diploma, UG degree and PG Degree.</p><p>He has developed number of educational programmes in the field of solar water pumping system, water management, watershed management and food safety & quality management at national level. Presently he is coordinating four programmes viz Bachelor of Science (Food Safety and Quality Management) (BSCFFSQM), Diploma in watershed Management (DWM), Diploma in Value Added Products from Fruits and Vegetables (DVAPFV), Certificate in Water Harvesting and Management (CWHM), Awareness Programme in Solar Water Pumping System (APSWP). He has published 50 research papers in peer reviewed national & international journals and participated in 38 national & international conferences. He has also contributed more than 22 book chapters and published three book and two extension manuals. He has organized number of national and international conferences as Organizing Secretary /Co-organizing Secretary/ member organizing committee. He has received Ph.D. Student Incentive Award-2012 award, Gold Medal-2014, Special Research Award-2016 and National Fellow-2019 from Soil Conservation Society of India. Fertilizer Association of India has awarded him with Golden Jubilee Award for Doctoral Research in Fertilizer Uses in 2013 for outstanding research work on dynamics of nutrient movement in soil under fertigation during Ph.D. He has also honored with University Silver Medal-2015 by the Indira Gandhi National Open University, New Delhi, India. Dr. Kumar is a life member of different professional societies and actively involved in Indian Society of Soil and Water Conservation, New Delhi. He was Joint Secretary and presently holding position of Treasure in Soil Conservation Society of India, New Delhi.</p></td>
